;; The appliance, plus a tunnel.
;;
;; A field device that is reachable from somewhere else: the simulated
;; device on Modbus, OPC UA, CAN and MQTT as before, with WireGuard so a
;; client can reach it across a network it is not on.
;;
;; The tunnel is the kernel's; feature:wireguard adds wg(8) and wg-quick(8)
;; to drive it. Configuration is /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf, which this image
;; deliberately does not carry: a private key baked into an image is a
;; private key everyone who flashes it shares.
;;
;; As a build this is the smallest thing worth caching: it extends
;; raspberrypi3-64-bringup by one package, so with that tree in the store
;; it is a minute rather than twenty.

(image raspberrypi3-64-vpn
  (compose
    image:raspberrypi3-64-bringup
    feature:wireguard)
  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
